{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>The beginning.</b> With patach of the heh of the building-pattern on account of the guttural letter, and likewise \"and I will testify to him with righteousness\" [the heh takes patach because of the guttural]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The lemma החלתי is rendered from its root meaning 'I began'; Ibn Ezra's point concerns the vocalization of the prefixed heh (patach rather than other vowels) due to the following guttural. The second example appears to quote a phrase, possibly an allusion to Psalm 50:7 or similar; rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:04.241416273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}